[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Characters"
brief_tooltip = "Captain: You control directly, provides morale aura.
Officers: Controllable units you command.
Men: AI-controlled, handle survival autonomously."
implemented = true
detailed_text = "[b]Three Ranks of Survivor[/b]

[i]The Royal Navy ran on strict hierarchy. Captain Crozier commanded Terror; his officers relayed orders; the able seamen did the work. That chain of command is all that stands between your men and chaos.[/i]

Your expedition consists of 30-45 crew divided into three ranks:

[b]Captain (You)[/b]
• You control the Captain directly at all times
• His presence steadies nearby men, boosting their morale
• If the Captain dies, the expedition is lost

[b]Officers[/b]
• A handful of lieutenants and mates you can give direct orders
• Useful for leading work parties, scouting, or managing specific tasks
• Fewer in number but more capable than ordinary seamen

[b]Men[/b]
• The bulk of your crew — they act on their own initiative
• They will seek food when hungry, warmth when cold, and rest when tired
• They gather materials and work at construction sites without being told
• You can override their decisions by giving them direct commands

[b]Traits[/b]
Each survivor has randomly assigned traits that shape his abilities:
• [b]Strong[/b] — Carries more, builds faster
• [b]Cold Blooded[/b] — Naturally resistant to cold
• [b]Navigator[/b] — Better at finding locations
• [b]Drunkard[/b] — Eats more, prone to mental breaks
• [b]Coward[/b] — Flees danger, lower morale
Double-click any man to see his traits and full condition.

[b]Death[/b]
When a survivor dies, his body remains where he fell. The sight damages the morale of those nearby. In desperate circumstances, the dead can be butchered for meat."
